  "suggestions": [
    "Event bus: Kafka recommended for durable async processing. In-memory fallback for dev/demo mode.",
    "Real-time: WebSocket for bidirectional, SSE for server push only.",
    "User interaction inferred: features require input triggers or status views \u2014 frontend included.",
    "Personas: Clinician, Patient, Nurse, Receptionist, Admin, Developer \u2014 acceptance criteria should be written from these perspectives.",
    "Compliance: HIPAA (US) \u2014 encryption at rest/transit, access audit logs, BAA with vendors, minimum necessary principle, breach notification",
    "Compliance: GDPR (EU) \u2014 consent management, data portability, right to deletion, DPO, DPIA for high-risk processing, 72h breach notice",
    "Compliance: FDA 21 CFR Part 11 (US) \u2014 electronic signature validation, audit trail integrity, system validation documentation",
    "Deployment: offline-first \u2014 Must work without continuous connectivity \u2014 local storage, sync on reconnect",
    "Deployment: multi-tenant \u2014 Tenant data isolation required \u2014 row-level security or schema-per-tenant",
    "Data: Protected Health Information (PHI) \u2014 encrypt at rest (AES-256) and in transit (TLS 1.2+), access logging, minimum necessary access, no logs/caches",
    "Data: Authentication Credentials (SECRET) \u2014 hash passwords (bcrypt cost>=12), env vars for secrets, rotate keys, never log or return in API responses",
    "Integrations: EHR/Clinical, Calendar/Scheduling, Analytics/Telemetry \u2014 design API contracts and error handling for each.",
    "Operations (auditability): required \u2014 immutable audit log, correlation IDs on all operations, who/what/when/why for mutations, tamper-evident storage"
  ],
